### World briefs — all routes require a session (run auth.http login first).
# Briefs are background for the classifier and selection prompts. Nothing
# refreshes them on a schedule: PUT one you wrote (e.g. drafted in a Claude
# chat with web search), or POST .../generate to have the backend research it.
# With the manual LLM relay running, generate lands in the relay queue.

@topic = INTERNATIONAL_CONFLICT
@pageSize = 20

### Live brief for every topic that has one
GET {{baseUrl}}/world-briefs

### Version history for one topic (offset pagination, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/world-briefs/{{topic}}/history?limit={{pageSize}}&offset=0

### Save a brief you wrote as the topic's new live version
# asOf (optional, defaults to now, never in the future) is when the facts were
# current; the prompt flags the brief stale after WORLD_BRIEF_STALE_AFTER_HOURS.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/world-briefs/{{topic}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "body": "Replace with the current state of play: who is doing what, what was threatened, paused or agreed (with absolute dates), pending deadlines and scheduled talks.",
    "sourceUrls": []
}

### Research the topic with web search and save the result (synchronous)
POST {{baseUrl}}/world-briefs/{{topic}}/generate
